  "conversation_name": "What intelligence makes possible, and who gets to steer it",
  "conversation_title": "What intelligence makes possible, and who gets to steer it",
  "executive_summary": "The conversation follows Aditya's account of finding room for curiosity, developing concerns about software incentives, and confronting AI systems whose usefulness exceeds his confidence in their explanation or control. A second sustained inquiry asks what inexpensive, moderately capable AI could change: conversation, research, learning, and communication across different experiences. Those possibilities expose tensions between personalization and trust, individual control and collective risk. The discussion ends with a tentative position on model access and an explicit invitation to continue, rather than a settled safety framework.",
