    {
      "id": "demo-m52",
      "node_name": "If systems improve themselves, release looks different",
      "summary": "Aditya also entertains a fast-takeoff scenario in which systems improve their own training or architecture and become difficult to control. He worries that open releases could intensify races and enable misuse.",
      "semantic_level": 1,
      "level": 1,
      "semantic_type": "chunk",
      "thread_id": null,
      "thread_label": null,
      "children_ids": [],
      "parent_id": "i23",
      "utterance_ids": [
        "baddf3c1-739d-4b54-8486-d1a671fa5008",
        "cce4f909-1498-4094-b809-95da8bd885a9",
        "9d603137-eab2-462f-83cd-9f82a3f75d44",
        "288e58b0-a584-48e5-b603-1939f126b3ba",
        "c5ebfc63-113f-4767-b15e-1979154c6a91",
        "5856ab34-3569-431b-9f56-7e4326da7866",
        "316d59cf-7dbb-47cb-b7e1-f79e346d2d03",
        "c04236b1-ba4e-4e43-b391-638cc686b688"
      ],
      "sequence_number": 52,
      "argument_role": "assumption",
      "source_ref": {
        "utterance_ids": [
          "baddf3c1-739d-4b54-8486-d1a671fa5008",
          "cce4f909-1498-4094-b809-95da8bd885a9",
          "9d603137-eab2-462f-83cd-9f82a3f75d44",
          "288e58b0-a584-48e5-b603-1939f126b3ba",
          "c5ebfc63-113f-4767-b15e-1979154c6a91",
          "5856ab34-3569-431b-9f56-7e4326da7866",
          "316d59cf-7dbb-47cb-b7e1-f79e346d2d03",
          "c04236b1-ba4e-4e43-b391-638cc686b688"
        ]
      },
      "source_turns": [
        {
          "id": "baddf3c1-739d-4b54-8486-d1a671fa5008",
          "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
          "sequence_number": 1194,
          "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
          "speaker_name": null,
          "speaker_source": "model",
          "speaker_confidence": null,
          "speaker_revision": 0,
          "text": "And we are very close to the fast takeoff world, a fast takeoff meaning that they're going to be starting to see the models start improving its own training methods, its own architecture.",
          "timestamp_start": 4686.72,
          "timestamp_end": 4696.72,
          "duration_seconds": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "cce4f909-1498-4094-b809-95da8bd885a9",
          "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
          "sequence_number": 1195,
          "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
          "speaker_name": null,
          "speaker_source": "model",
          "speaker_confidence": null,
          "speaker_revision": 0,
          "text": "its own architecture and it's going to start writing code for itself and it'll quickly",
          "timestamp_start": 4696.72,
          "timestamp_end": 4701.4400000000005,
          "duration_seconds": 4.720000000000255
        },
        {
          "id": "9d603137-eab2-462f-83cd-9f82a3f75d44",
          "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
          "sequence_number": 1196,
          "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
          "speaker_name": null,
          "speaker_source": "model",
          "speaker_confidence": null,
          "speaker_revision": 0,
          "text": "become super intelligent and then it'll lose control over it'll become like an autonomous",
          "timestamp_start": 4701.4400000000005,
          "timestamp_end": 4707.16,
          "duration_seconds": 5.719999999999345
        },
        {
          "id": "288e58b0-a584-48e5-b603-1939f126b3ba",
          "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
          "sequence_number": 1197,
          "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
          "speaker_name": null,
          "speaker_source": "model",
          "speaker_confidence": null,
          "speaker_revision": 0,
          "text": "system that we can no longer debug or control in any sense.",
          "timestamp_start": 4707.16,
          "timestamp_end": 4711.96,
          "duration_seconds": 4.800000000000182
        },
        {
          "id": "c5ebfc63-113f-4767-b15e-1979154c6a91",
          "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
          "sequence_number": 1198,
          "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
          "speaker_name": null,
          "speaker_source": "model",
          "speaker_confidence": null,
          "speaker_revision": 0,
          "text": "In which case open source might be the reason that these companies are racing towards building",
          "timestamp_start": 4711.96,
          "timestamp_end": 4718.96,
          "duration_seconds": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "5856ab34-3569-431b-9f56-7e4326da7866",
          "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
          "sequence_number": 1199,
          "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
          "speaker_name": null,
          "speaker_source": "model",
          "speaker_confidence": null,
          "speaker_revision": 0,
          "text": "larger and larger models and even if the top players agree to test thoroughly before deploying",
          "timestamp_start": 4718.96,
          "timestamp_end": 4727.18,
          "duration_seconds": 8.220000000000255
        },
        {
          "id": "316d59cf-7dbb-47cb-b7e1-f79e346d2d03",
          "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
          "sequence_number": 1200,
          "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
          "speaker_name": null,
          "speaker_source": "model",
          "speaker_confidence": null,
          "speaker_revision": 0,
          "text": "it, the open-source models will not even use it for anything they want.",
          "timestamp_start": 4727.18,
          "timestamp_end": 4731.18,
          "duration_seconds": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "c04236b1-ba4e-4e43-b391-638cc686b688",
          "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
          "sequence_number": 1201,
          "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
          "speaker_name": null,
          "speaker_source": "model",
          "speaker_confidence": null,
          "speaker_revision": 0,
          "text": "So we're going to be seeing a lot more of bad use cases.",
          "timestamp_start": 4731.18,
          "timestamp_end": 4735.28,
          "duration_seconds": 4.099999999999454
        }
      ],
      "source_excerpt": "And we are very close to the fast takeoff world, a fast takeoff meaning that they're going to be starting to see the models start improving its own training methods, its own architecture.",
      "provenance_utterance_ids": [
        "baddf3c1-739d-4b54-8486-d1a671fa5008",
        "cce4f909-1498-4094-b809-95da8bd885a9",
        "9d603137-eab2-462f-83cd-9f82a3f75d44",
        "288e58b0-a584-48e5-b603-1939f126b3ba",
        "c5ebfc63-113f-4767-b15e-1979154c6a91",
        "5856ab34-3569-431b-9f56-7e4326da7866",
        "316d59cf-7dbb-47cb-b7e1-f79e346d2d03",
        "c04236b1-ba4e-4e43-b391-638cc686b688"
      ],
      "timestamp_start": 4686.72,
      "timestamp_end": 4735.28,
      "memberships": [
        {
          "parent_id": "i23",
          "role": "shared",
          "explanation": "A fast-takeoff scenario supplies a contrasting argument about races and loss of control."
        }
      ],
      "thread_ids": [
        "t13"
      ],
      "provenance_source_ref": {
