      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "line to try to extrapolate how this curve might look like so the parameters is used here is the",
      "timestamp_start": 1642.76,
      "timestamp_end": 1647.9599999999998,
      "duration_seconds": 5.199999999999818
    },
    {
      "id": "432ed520-fe75-4c21-9cf4-b8fc29420ef6",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 412,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "number of degrees of freedom that you have like if you have a single variable a single parameter",
      "timestamp_start": 1647.9599999999998,
      "timestamp_end": 1652.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.320000000000164
    },
    {
      "id": "13893122-8f99-4227-a15d-fba61a38fae2",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 413,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "it's like y is equal to mx plus c or mx then m is the only parameter the only free variable",
      "timestamp_start": 1652.28,
      "timestamp_end": 1658.1999999999998,
      "duration_seconds": 5.919999999999845
    },
    {
      "id": "5829e0a8-6b82-40d3-8a3f-8bd2ea1d2d96",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 414,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "which can be varied so depending on the different values of m that line will have different slopes",
      "timestamp_start": 1658.1999999999998,
      "timestamp_end": 1662.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.560000000000173
    },
    {
      "id": "ac9d67f1-6531-42f1-b7a3-8ec67f4a4c9d",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 415,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "And then if you have MX plus C, then you can also adjust the lines intercepted with the X axis.",
      "timestamp_start": 1662.76,
      "timestamp_end": 1667.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "54640e8d-7e37-47b7-8bd5-eb1918607368",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 416,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "And if you have X square, AX square plus BX plus C, if you have like a second order polynomial, then you have two or three parameters.",
      "timestamp_start": 1667.76,
      "timestamp_end": 1675.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "e89f4e46-f499-4a51-ab0f-b5e21afe6bbd",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 417,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "So when I say these models have a lot of parameters, I'm trying to say that they have a lot of degrees of freedom.",
      "timestamp_start": 1675.76,
      "timestamp_end": 1680.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "7273b238-5891-46bb-bd99-75531797a56a",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 418,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "It's a high dimensional function that is being fitted.",
      "timestamp_start": 1680.76,
      "timestamp_end": 1684.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "bf31f8c4-8518-47a7-8cfa-b2d05fb2e2b1",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 419,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "We're trying to- Billions of parameters.",
      "timestamp_start": 1684.76,
      "timestamp_end": 1688.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "bece80cd-a6f8-42b3-a15b-5f99039db26c",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 420,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "of parameters and there are theorems mathematically that show that these are universal function",
      "timestamp_start": 1688.76,
      "timestamp_end": 1693,
      "duration_seconds": 4.240000000000009
    },
    {
      "id": "bc14c4b6-22e3-424f-bc5e-73578c755881",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 421,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "approximators that you can approximate any function so how you train this is that you",
      "timestamp_start": 1693,
      "timestamp_end": 1697.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7999999999999545
    },
    {
      "id": "0727ca32-eb0f-4306-9fc1-0be7681d00d1",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 422,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "take this architecture which is known as a transform architecture with attention heads",
      "timestamp_start": 1697.8,
      "timestamp_end": 1702.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.240000000000009
    },
    {
      "id": "8b7ba227-77fb-44ef-b61c-9b8d7aa2fcf5",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 423,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "and i can go into depth if you want but the basic idea here is just at a high level right",
      "timestamp_start": 1702.04,
      "timestamp_end": 1707.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.920000000000073
    },
    {
      "id": "b270ea60-beb2-4ddd-8a91-44468a351c5c",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 424,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "it's a black box the idea is what you're doing here is you're showing it",
      "timestamp_start": 1710.28,
      "timestamp_end": 1713.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0399999999999636
    },
    {
      "id": "13a39396-7eb0-4d15-a65a-2899a5d04b9c",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 425,
      "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
      "speaker_name": null,
      "speaker_source": "model",
      "speaker_confidence": null,
      "speaker_revision": 0,
      "text": "every single document in the internet, like every single high quality text that's been",
      "timestamp_start": 1713.32,
      "timestamp_end": 1720.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.400000000000091
    },
    {
      "id": "8ac1beb1-dc82-4360-ad45-fe2df092f1dd",
      "conversation_id": "3fc4885e-a1b3-484e-9c9f-05e51557b9ba",
      "sequence_number": 426,
